   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Meeting up and the near future",
     "texto": [
      "To suggest a plan, use **quedar**:\n\n- **¿Quedamos el sábado?**\n- **Quedamos a las seis en el café.**\n\nAnd to talk about a plan in the near future, use **ir a + infinitivo**:\n\n- **Voy a estudiar.** (it is not the present, it is what I will do)\n- **¿Qué vas a hacer mañana?**\n\nNote: the verb that changes is **ir** (voy, vas, va…); the other verb stays in the infinitive."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Ir a + infinitive",
     "texto": [
      "The near future is formed with **ir** + **a** + infinitive:\n\n- **Voy a estudiar** esta tarde.\n- **Vas a venir** mañana.\n- **Vamos a ver** una película.\n\nIt is the most natural way to talk about nearby plans. The future with -é («estudiaré») exists, but it sounds more formal.\n\nAnd a very useful phrase for making an excuse: **Es que…** → «Es que trabajo»."
     ],
